{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106847-how-often-do-your-dragon-blooded-characters-invest-in-most-of-their-aspect-abilities","id":1106847,"title":"How often do your Dragon-Blooded characters invest in MOST of their Aspect Abilities?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-22T20:30:13-07:00","id":1106847,"title":"How often do your Dragon-Blooded characters invest in MOST of their Aspect Abilities?","content":"As the title asks.<br /> <br /> How often do you see or play Dragon-Blooded who only really invest into their Favored Abilities and one or two of their Aspect Abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T20:41:20-07:00","id":1106854,"title":"","content":"Well, the 2e DB game I played the ST said we should be well rounded, but then turned around and talked and talked and talked about combat abilities. Which happened every thee to five months. After awhile I was going for eats, drinks and chitty-chat, and eventually quit even that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T23:41:28-07:00","id":1106901,"title":"","content":"The largest ratio I've seen of Aspect Ability dots to Ability dots is in Fire Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T06:28:05-07:00","id":1106989,"title":"","content":"For my Dawn character, his character development has pushed him to develop non-Caste/Favored abilities further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13507-nicklance","name":"NickLance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T07:57:23-07:00","id":1107014,"title":"","content":"I tend to play Air aspects as polyglot ninja sorcerers, so for me the answer is &quot;usually.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:57:10-07:00","id":1107043,"title":"","content":"In my Dragon Blooded games, I found that players of Wood and Water Aspects tended to invest heavily outside of their Aspect Abilities more than players of Air or Fire Aspects. Earth players seemed to go either way depending on character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-23-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:06:42-07:00","id":1107060,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with that for the most part.<br /> Most fire Aspects are combat/social characters, so happily take the 2 combat abilities and 2 social abilities (and maybe a bit of athletics). Though War is often popular.<br /> And 90% of Air aspects are sorcerers who are happy to take Thrown (it wasn't in 2.5, but in 2nd it was one of the strongest combat abilities for DBs), or ninjas who know Occult anyway because why not (and you want Linguistics for codes). Though Dodge is a pretty common (and, I think, fitting) favoured ability.<br /> <br /> In my experience, half of Wood aspects are woodsmen who heavily invest in wood abilities, but the other half are socialites who take Performance and not much of the other stuff.<br /> <br /> Water Aspects... if they're spies they take a lot of Water abilities, if they're pirates it's much more varied.<br /> <br /> Earth Aspects I have no idea because no-one ever seems to play them. But I assume they'd be keen not to spend all their stuff on Earth Aspect abilities because they're so passive.<br /> <br /> But saying all this? Honestly, a lot of my DB characters (and I've played a lot) started with 3 favoured abilities at 5, and 3-4 caste abilities at 5. You're just so heavily incentivised by the system to do it (especially when you have to take 1-2 dots in a bunch of stuff for your education anyway).<br /> I mean, the most optimal thing would be to have 7 abilities at 5 and 1 at 4 I guess, but generally speaking there's one aspect ability that doesn't fit the character.*<br /> <br /> So anyway, at that point you're filling all of them up anyway, so there's not really much divide.<br /> <br /> I think the only time I had a character who had 3 favoured abilities at 5 and very little in his aspect abilities is when I deliberately said &quot;I'm going to have a character who doesn't fit his aspect.&quot; He was a Fire-Aspected bureaucrat from Sesus. But that was only because I did it deliberately.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying this, I played a ton of Dragonblood games in 2nd ed, not so much in 2.5. Maybe it changed. And I'd be less obsessed with optimising character gen than when I was a younger roleplayer (although saying that, the current Exalted game I play is at nearly 400xp, so if I did retire my Solar and play a DB as I probably will once Arms is out, I might as well have a ton of abilities at 5).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Sunder, was there a particular reason you asked, or just general curiosity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-23-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T14:20:22-07:00","id":1107122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106847-how-often-do-your-dragon-blooded-characters-invest-in-most-of-their-aspect-abilities?p=1107060#post1107060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, Sunder, was there a particular reason you asked, or just general curiosity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even before 3rd Edition made playing a Dragon-Blood seem more fun and exciting than ever, I made it a time-killing hobby or time-killer to sort characters from other media by Exalted Host and Caste/Aspect.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Aspects have <i>always </i>been the hardest, because of Aspect Abilities. More than any other splat, it seems that you end up with too many Abilities that don't fit the concept and not quite enough Favored Abilities to make up the gap. Sure, things are fairly painless if the character naturally fits the Fire Aspect, but most anything else involves stretching and squeezing.<br /> <br /> Solar Castes are mapped to human archetypes, but Terrestrial Aspects are not as concerned with the human element.<br /> <br /> That's why I was hopeful that the expansion of Solar Caste Abilities would also apply to Dragon-Blooded Aspects, <i>at least </i>for the purpose of letting them substitute their native Aspect attack Ability (War for Earth) with any other attack Ability (or War, for non-Earth Aspects who would rather be a rear-line strategist).<br /> <br /> Because, it makes sense that most of the Dragon-Blooded PCs of a sail-based adventure would be Water Aspects and need to find ways other than Aspect to distinguish their characters from each other, and one of the ways that would make the most sense is &quot;how they hit people&quot;. It seems odd that the vast majority of Dragon-Blooded sailors would do battle on the high seas <i>with their fists</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But saying all this? Honestly, a lot of my DB characters (and I've played a lot) started with 3 favoured abilities at 5, and 3-4 caste abilities at 5. You're just so heavily incentivised by the system to do it </div> </div> </div>And by &quot;do it&quot;, you mean &quot;invest dots into Aspect Abilities that don't reflect what I want to do with the character&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T16:26:35-07:00","id":1107146,"title":"","content":"... Kind of, yes.<br /> It's not quite as bad as that sounds: often it was stuff that's useful for the character (I mean, having Dodge 5 is useful for almost any 2nd ed DB, especially at Essence 4+). If it was something that really went against the character concept, I wouldn't take it (for example, Socialise 5 with the rough-mannered breeding 0 outcaste I played once), but when the game rewards you for starting with as many abilities at 5 as you can (alternatively, you can take 5 abilities at 5 and 10 dots of specialties in favoured/aspect abilities, I did that once), and you have all these ability dots and freebies to fill stuff with anyway (35 dots of abilities is a lot, and with 12 points of backgrounds about 3/4 of characters don't want to put more freebies there), it kind of encourages you to go &quot;well, my air-aspected sorcerer could have learned a bunch of languages, sure, and maybe she loved sneaking around the Heptagram... dunno what else I'd put it anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> But. That's not really a good way to design a character.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, I resist that temptation, because it's silly, and I found the game's incentive-system was encouraging me to make characters that weren't always as fun as I'd have made without it, but that might also be because the Exalted games I play now are far less lethal than back in 2nd ed anyway, so I'm not worried about my character being weak and getting hit in the face with a grand goremaul.*<br /> (Of course, I say this, but actually there's still not much else I want to spend freebies on anyway, especially now virtues are gone and you get more points of merits, so why not spend all the freebies on abilities?)<br /> <br /> *The previously-mentioned one character I took who did only have 1-2 dots in his Aspect abilities. Not having Dodge or Melee 5 is not helpful when an angry Earth aspect wants to punish you for having different musical tastes to him, and his punishment is grand goremaul-based.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. To go back to your reason for asking on this thread: I have seen DB characters who've had, say, 5 dots in 3 favoured abilities and only 2 aspect abilities, with just 0-2 dots in the other 3, but I've never, ever, seen a DB who needed more than 3 favoured abilities for their concept.<br /> Plenty of characters I'm sure wouldn't have minded having it, but actually needed? No.<br /> People's concepts often subconsciously/naturally seque into their aspect (fire-aspected swordsmen are much more common than water-aspected swordsmen), but when they don't, most character concepts only require 2-3 abilities at 5. I mean, they might require a bit of other abilities, but not generally so much that they need 4 favoureds.<br /> I guess the closest I saw was a Wood Aspect socialite who favoured Presence, Socialise (and I don't remember the third one). I guess she'd want to then have Integrity and a defensive ability. But did she actually need to favour Dodge and Integrity? Not really. Integrity 3 and a couple of charms would be fine (especially as Socialise had Jaded Defence in anyway).<br /> <br /> Could I ask what sort of concepts you came up with that needed 4 favoured abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-23-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:01:52-07:00","id":1107459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106847-how-often-do-your-dragon-blooded-characters-invest-in-most-of-their-aspect-abilities?p=1107146#post1107146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Kind of, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well dots are only half the story here, really. If you have 5 melee and 5 stealth and you have no melee charms and the entire DB stealth tree you're definitely way more invested in stealth than melee. In this way I usually found people who might have more dots in their favoured end up having more charms in aspect.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, more to what Sunder is getting at, yes DB aspects are very restrictive. They're kind of the opposite end of the spectrum from the freedom that Solars have. This means that you're absolutely going to have a hard time porting characters over from other media, in particular because the exaltation, at least as of 2e, affects your personality.<br /> <br /> The aspects aren't loose archetypes of heroes they're more like rigid job descriptions, in comparison kind of like this.<br /> <br /> Solars:<br /> Dawn - Invincible warrior hero<br /> Zenith - Unstoppable inspiration and leader<br /> Twilight - Genius in all things<br /> Night - Shadow who can move anywhere through the world<br /> Eclipse - World walker and communicator<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded:<br /> Air - Warrior scribe<br /> Earth - General and builder<br /> Fire - Warrior socialite<br /> Water - Merchant and law-maker/breaker<br /> Wood - Wild ranger<br /> <br /> Even looking at the charms in the abilities that don't seem to fit those archetypes so rigidly you tend to see a common theme. For example archery allows you to use plants to form arrows and integrity's ability to bolster troops and allies to inhuman feats of stamina. <br /> <br /> Now what I think will change in the next edition is that if you favour a combat ability you won't be penalized for it. I mean the lore basically already treats the world as such, I think more DBS have out of aspect combat abilities than in aspect ones. So what that will let you do is be a warrior scribe who's a bit of a ranger, or a sailor, or uses a sword, and you should be fine. <br /> <br /> On the other hand if you're wanting to do what a twilight can do, and be a genius inventor who wields his personally forged daiklave from horseback, you might be stepping too far out of your role and gonna have a bad time. If that's what you're looking for I'd suggest taking a blue jade weapon and investing heavily in wind/Lightning evocations if that's what you're wanting out of the character/port.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T02:47:10-07:00","id":1107589,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a good point about charms. When I played say, Sesus Iyushi the violent and irreverent Air sorcerer, I think I had Socialise 5, but only one Socialise charm, so it wasn't really that much of an investment.<br /> <br /> And I've certainly seen a lot of DB characters who've got 3 favoured abilities at 5, and 4-5 aspect abilities at 5, but their charms were all out of the 3 favoured and 2-3 of their aspect abilities. Like, I think V'neef Valkor, our party's wood aspect archer, had all the Dodge charms (as did pretty much everyone else!) but only one or two performance charms and no ride charms, though I think he had the abilities at a high level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, more to what Sunder is getting at, yes DB aspects are very restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this I'm not so sure of.<br /> I never saw anyone have big difficulties with the fact there were only 3 favoured abilities. In fact, most people seemed to find DBs <i>less</i> restrictive than Solars, because pretty much everyone's basic aspect abilities already included a social ability and a combat ability, whereas, say, a 2nd ed Eclipse would often want to buy a combat ability, maybe Dodge, and 3 more social abilities, probably Occult, and they've already run out of favoured abilities. Which is why the less restrictive caste abilities of 3rd ed is so important.<br /> <br /> No, the big restriction was the extra mote on out-of-aspect. That's why everyone used the combat ability of their own aspect (which maybe is why no-one played Earth Aspects...), or an aspected Martial Art.<br /> I guess maybe if that's gone, suddenly you'll get loads of people wanting to play Air-aspected swordsmen or fire-aspected brawlers or Wood-Aspects throwing boomerangs, or whatever, and it may be more awkward.<br /> <br /> But even so, 3 favoured abilities seems plenty. I mean, in your above example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand if you're wanting to do what a twilight can do, and be a genius inventor who wields his personally forged daiklave from horseback, you might be stepping too far out of your role and gonna have a bad time. If that's what you're looking for I'd suggest taking a blue jade weapon and investing heavily in wind/Lightning evocations if that's what you're wanting out of the character/port.</div> </div> </div> </div>Air aspect gets Lore and Occult. Your favoured abilities are Craft/Melee/Ride. Surely that's covered it?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not saying that if DBs got 5 favoured abilities it would horrify me. Just that I've never seen a problem with it in all the DB games I've played. And I like the way DBs are more focused/restrictive: in my experience, it actually makes it easier for most players to design an interesting DB character (not everyone, but most people).<br /> <br /> (Of course, I'd also not be horrified if no one had any caste or aspect or favoured abilities, but that's just me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2017, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T03:55:09-07:00","id":1107599,"title":"","content":"I recall a time that Holden suggested that Dragon Blooded were reasonably flexible, because Aspect Abilities tended to be rather diverse.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, as an example, you've got Earth Aspects. Think of the archetypes that can emerge from any one of those Abilities, and the permutations you can get from several of them; I think some diverse qualities can come out of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106847-how-often-do-your-dragon-blooded-characters-invest-in-most-of-their-aspect-abilities?p=1107459#post1107459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The aspects aren't loose archetypes of heroes they're more like rigid job descriptions, in comparison kind of like this.<br /> <br /> Solars:<br /> Dawn - Invincible warrior hero<br /> Zenith - Unstoppable inspiration and leader<br /> Twilight - Genius in all things<br /> Night - Shadow who can move anywhere through the world<br /> Eclipse - World walker and communicator<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded:<br /> Air - Warrior scribe<br /> Earth - General and builder<br /> Fire - Warrior socialite<br /> Water - Merchant and law-maker/breaker<br /> Wood - Wild ranger</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that could be disputed as what the actual books depicted even in the prior Editions, but what's important is what they're doing now, where Aspect is more a matter of bodily and emotional expressions.<br /> <br /> Do you remember how the core book described the Dragon Blooded Aspects?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T05:18:28-07:00","id":1107603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106847-how-often-do-your-dragon-blooded-characters-invest-in-most-of-their-aspect-abilities?p=1107599#post1107599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall a time that Holden suggested that Dragon Blooded were reasonably flexible, because Aspect Abilities tended to be rather diverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable to me, and is generally my experience of playing DBs vs playing Solars. I guess it does kind of &quot;push&quot; you towards particular abilities, but then, that's kind of the point.<br /> (I mean, you decide you want to play a socialite from House Cynis. You choose the Wood aspect, and favour Integrity, Presence and Socialise. You think &quot;oh I guess I need some kind of combat ability, I guess I'd better pick Archery since it's an Aspect ability, rather than Melee or whatever.&quot; But then, that's the point: as a Wood Aspect, you're supposed to be incentivised towards Archery. But if your original concept was of a Wood Aspect who doesn't use Archery but uses, say, boomerangs, then you don't have to take Archery, you do have the option for 3 non-Wood abilities. But Archery is there for those who don't have a strong preference.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI think that could be disputed as what the actual books depicted even in the prior Editions, but what's important is what they're doing now, where Aspect is more a matter of bodily and emotional expressions. </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I think that thinking of it this way leads to more interesting characters. From the, oh, 20+ DB PCs I saw in 2nd ed, I'd say they were generally chosen because the player felt the &quot;feel&quot; of the Aspect fit the character, more than they saw it as an appropriate &quot;job&quot; like with Solars. The young ambitious officer was a Fire Aspect, because of his fiery personality. The monk with the rather flexible and liberal view of theology was a Water Aspect. The strategic general who loved flying on his magitech wings and was obssed with airships, was an Air Aspect. The decadent socialite who loved sex, drugs, and experiencing all of life's pleasures, was a Wood aspect.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, they just picked the Aspect that was most common in the House. Which is an interesting thing you can do with Aspects that you can't do with Castes: the character has power that <i>doesn't</i> fit with their abilities and ambitions.<br /> For example, I played a bureucrat from House Sesus. He was intelligent but had no great aptitude for combat. Then, like both his parents before him, he exalted as a Fire Aspect, and found that combat and socialising began to come easier to him.<br /> Or, you could play a timid and sickly young noble who gains the strength and fortitude of stone, giving him confidence and inner strength.<br /> Or a regular farmboy who suddenly gains an incredible aptitude for kung-fu due to his Water exaltation.<br /> Or a sailor in the Pelleps fleet who finds that she has an incredible bond with the wood of the ship, rather than the waves.<br /> Or whatever.<br /> I think that leads to a lot of interesting character development that's not so easy to do with a Celestial, whose exaltations reflect what they already are (or at least, already had the potential to be).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, of course, there'll be more support for this now, as with the different Aspected charms, an Air swordsman and a Wood swordsman are likely going to be expressing their skills in rather different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2017, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:26:30-07:00","id":1107629,"title":"","content":"Posted this in the wrong thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107587#post1107587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I remembering correctly that Vance said he thought the best thing to do with education, rather than the old system of extra ability dots but compulsory stuff, was some specialties? Like you get some free specialties if you're a Dynast, some different ones if you're from Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could mean that instead of 35 Ability dots to distribute, you could only have the same 28 available to Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Which would further pinch Dragon-Blooded character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:44:13-07:00","id":1107666,"title":"","content":"I dunno how apt this is, but I had a concept for a Sky Pirate type Exalt in an alternative Creation. Airships and biplane ahoy.<br /> <br /> I wanted to make someone REALLY at home in the skies. I figured Air aspect made sense. So I started thinking about what abilities would be most important to someone whose idea of a fun time is &quot;Jump off the side of an airship, grapple into the side of another, and attack the crew of the other ship&quot;<br /> <br /> So I figured that would require investment in Melee, Athletics, maybe some Dodge, a bit of Presence for intimidation upon landing...<br /> <br /> Then I realized that while Air fit her personality, mechanically? I would be shafting myself making her anything BUT a Fire Aspect.<br /> <br /> Which is why the promise of multi-element Abilities is so exciting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:50:30-07:00","id":1107669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106847-how-often-do-your-dragon-blooded-characters-invest-in-most-of-their-aspect-abilities?p=1107666#post1107666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno how apt this is, but I had a concept for a Sky Pirate type Exalt in an alternative Creation. Airships and biplane ahoy.<br /> <br /> I wanted to make someone REALLY at home in the skies. I figured Air aspect made sense. So I started thinking about what abilities would be most important to someone whose idea of a fun time is &quot;Jump off the side of an airship, grapple into the side of another, and attack the crew of the other ship&quot;<br /> <br /> So I figured that would require investment in Melee, Athletics, maybe some Dodge, a bit of Presence for intimidation upon landing...<br /> <br /> Then I realized that while Air fit her personality, mechanically? I would be shafting myself making her anything BUT a Fire Aspect.<br /> <br /> Which is why the promise of multi-element Abilities is so exciting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You'd still be best served making the character Fire Aspect, but at least you could choose as many Air-aspected Charms as you could find within the Fire Aspect Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:36:56-07:00","id":1107743,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd suggest sticking with Air: what really shafts you mechanically is when your Fire Aspect tries jumping off an airship, fluffs the roll, falls a mile and goes splat. Not a problem for Air Aspects!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T23:23:32-07:00","id":1107914,"title":"","content":"Initially I went with what felt right for the character even if I ended up dependent upon Martial Arts or Sorcery but long-term I tend to work on Aspect abilities because they're there unless they are completely useless to me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}